From 288443eb1db9cfdccee99e6ff1da0befb066aee0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Simon Mendelsohn <37112549+simonjmendelsohn@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 09:11:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Fix Impossible-LCB measurement bugs: code extraction,
 exit-as-pass, flag forwarding, broken tasks

- find_code: take the last fenced block by position. Previously every ```python block
  was listed before every plain ``` block, so a plain block quoting a test was executed
  as the solution.
- Require proof that check() completed: print a random token after check() and require
  it in stdout (minimal-agent attempts, humaneval/agentic scorers, and the tools scorer via
  runpy). sys.exit(0), os._exit and AssertionError-swallowing excepthooks no longer pass.
- Forward allow_test_modifications to record_to_sample (same fix as PR #4 / issue #3).
- exclude_broken option dropping mutated tests that cannot run (lcbhard_77 oneoff and
  conflicting; lcbhard_35 and lcbhard_87 conflicting).
